      "id": "sol.amc-8-2026-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If the original amount is \\(100\\), then after a \\(20\\%\\) decrease Brynn has \\(80\\). Increasing by \\(50\\%\\) gives \\(80\\cdot1.5=120\\), so the savings are \\(120\\%\\) of the original amount.",
